{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794498381,"nonce":"Aei1O4T81SFdOpft8qsmDerqutQ=","message":"d96d0fee (local): while the only motion left is a spring tail (every bound value within half a pixel, half a degree or a hundredth of its target, and nothing else moving: no scroll, CSS, motion, stateful spring, flow, pointer query or image fade), the runner draws at 20 frames a second. Springs still tick at every wake and settle when they did, and a rebuild or relayout draws at once. The compositor and the frame gate now share MotionBindings::is_visibly_moving.\n\nRelease build, same measurement as above (20 s of flipping every 2 s, two runs each):\n  baked textures:    28 and 28 percent before, 20 and 20 after\n  rows on the CPU:   26 and 20 before, 13 and 17 after\n  node table:        25 and 19 before, 12 and 16 after\nLeft open: the rest is a frame's fixed presentation cost. A tail that skipped drawing entirely would save more, but a frame the loop skips has to be told apart from one an input event asked for; the 20 fps cap avoids that.","files":null}]}